// The landing at Hollin, at night: a ferry, and two people waiting for it.
cast:
  ada    "Ada"    — keeps the ferry
    [gender feminine]
  otto   "Otto"   — a pedlar, going over for the fair
    [gender masculine]
extras: a boy

facts (player):
  coins: int from 0 to 9   (game)
  carrying: set of lantern, needles
facts:
  rain: one of pouring, easing, stopped   (game)
  near: set of otto, boy   (game)   // who is standing by the player
  asked_price: bool
  trust: int from -3 to 3   // what Otto makes of you
  talked_down: bool

extern:
  crossings_left() -> int
  pay(int)
  give(ref of item)
  talk_down(who: ref of person, coins: int) -> bool (action)

== landing
  [music rain_on_water] [picture landing_night]
{ rain = pouring }
  Rain on the river, hard enough to hiss.
    [sound rain_heavy]
{ else }
  Rain on the river, thinning.
A lantern on a post, and a boat tied up under it.
A BOY: Ferry! Last ferry over!
OTTO: She heard you the first time.
ADA (without looking up): { rain = pouring: I go when the rain eases. Not before. | Nearly. Give it a minute. }
{ crossings_left() = 1 } ADA: And that's the last crossing tonight.
- (ask)
Otto {cycle: hums to himself | counts the buttons on his coat | looks at the sky}.
* How much to cross?
  [asked_price = true]
  ADA: Two coins. Same as always.
  -> ask
* { asked_price and coins < 2 } I haven't got two coins.
  You count what you have: {coins as one: one coin | other: {coins} coins}.
  ADA: Then you'd better find some more.
  You look at Otto.
  OTTO: Don't look at me.
    [trust -= 1]
  -> ask
* { asked_price and coins = 1 } Offer her the one coin you have.
  [talked_down = talk_down(ada, 1)]
  { talked_down }
    ADA: One, then. Don't tell the boy.
    [pay(1)]
    -> crossing
  ADA: Two. I don't haggle in the rain.
  -> ask
+ Look at the river.
  {seq: Black water, moving fast under the rain. | Still black. Still moving. | The river is not going anywhere, and nor, it seems, are you.}
  -> waiting ->
  -> ask
* Sit with Otto.
  You sit down beside him on the wet bench.
  OTTO: You'll want this, over there.
    [pause 1.5]
    [trust += 1]
  He puts a tin lantern in your hands.
  [give(lantern)] [carrying += lantern]
  -> ask
* { coins >= 2 and rain != pouring } Pay, and get in.
  [marked]
  [pay(2)]
  { not asked_price } ADA: Two coins, first.
  ADA: Mind the step.
  -> crossing
* Go home.
  You turn up the lane, the way the boy went.
  -> end

// what someone standing by says while the player waits
== waiting (pool)
= boy             when { near has boy }
  A BOY: Ferry! Ferry!
= boy_in_rain     when { near has boy and rain = pouring }
  A BOY: It's hardly raining at all!
= otto            when { near has otto }
  OTTO: My feet have gone to sleep.
= otto_kind       when { near has otto and trust > 0 }
  OTTO: Come back from the edge, will you. You're making me nervous.
= nobody
  Nobody says anything. The rain says enough.

== crossing
  [music oars]
The boat pushes off. Behind you the lantern on the post grows small.
-> midstream

= midstream
  [picture fog]
  Halfway over, the fog comes down{once: , and the far bank is gone}.
  -> lamp ->
  OTTO: I can't see the bank.
  ADA: You don't need to. I do.
  * Hold still.
    -> landfall
  * Stand up to look.
    The boat tips. Ada says something you are glad not to have heard.
    -> midstream

= landfall
  The keel scrapes on stones.
  ADA: Out you get.
  -> far_bank

== lamp
{ carrying has lantern }
  You hold up Otto's lantern. It makes a small room of light in the fog.
  <-
Ada's lantern swings at the prow, and lights nothing.
<-

== far_bank
  [music fair_far_off] [picture far_bank]
Mud, a path, and up the hill the lights of the fair.
{shuffle: A dog barks somewhere up the hill. | Someone at the fair is singing, badly. | A cart goes by with its lamps unlit.}
OTTO: Well. That's me.
{ trust > 0 } OTTO: Keep the lantern.
ADA: Tell {otto as masculine: him | feminine: her | other: them} the dogs up there bite.
-> end
